From e8cd1c3860fcb061af27ca0acedb4bfeb9356399 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Morse <james.morse@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:54:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH OLK-6.6 v5 02/18] dt-bindings: Rename the description of cpu
 nodes cpu.yaml

maillist inclusion
category: feature
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/9826

Reference: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20211015161416.2196-1-james.morse@arm.com/t/#u

--------------------------------

The cpus.yaml file describes the cpu nodes, not the cpus node.
Rename it to allow integration properties of all the cpus to be described
in the cpus node.

Also update the in-tree references to the renamed file. They describe CPU
node properties, so they must point at cpu.yaml; left alone they would
resolve to the cpus container node added later in this series.

Signed-off-by: James Morse <james.morse@arm.com>
Signed-off-by: Fanhua Li <lifanhua5@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Jiacheng Yu <yujiacheng3@huawei.com>
---
Changes in v3:
 - update the six references to the CPU node binding, from arm/cpus.yaml
   to arm/cpu.yaml
